"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152206683708_34f6b5d3", "type": "Claim", "text": "The large‑model survey in Acta Automatica Sinica (2025, 51(1):1–19, 
doi:10.16383/j.aas.c240542) introduces a simplified technical stack for general embodied intelligence robots comprising ‘brain’, ‘cerebellum’,
and ‘body’, where the body technology is relatively mature but becomes significantly more complex and costly when high‑degree‑of‑freedom 
elements such as dexterous hands are added, placing greater demands on high‑speed communication and computation.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], "citations": [5], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": "20260702152206745904_0cd0af28", "type": "Claim", "text": "Another white paper identifies composite 
multi-mode robots as a distinct technical route within embodied intelligence, arguing that multi-form-factor design and implementation are 
both a natural direction of robotics technology and a market-driven choice, and that such composite robots are actively promoting embodied 
intelligence.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], "citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855785973_336d63ca", 
"title": "大模型赋能的具身智能：自主决策和具身学习技术的全面最新综述-人工智能技术与咨询", "url": "https://www.longtengyatai.com/info/284", 
"source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-10-31T14:57:20"}]}, {"id": "20260702152206817777_f56df601", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 
technical evolution route of embodied intelligence described in a 2024–2025 industry report starts from traditional model-based and 
learning-based motion control and transitions to a ‘large model + robot’ paradigm, in which large language models handle task understanding 
and automatic code generation, vision–language models handle semantic environment understanding, and vision–language–action models generate 
end-to-end action policies.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152206889056_adb64068", "type": "Claim", "text": "End-to-end transformer-based vision–language–action control models such as Google 
Robotics’ RT-1 constitute a major technical route for embodied intelligence, achieving high success rates and semantic generalization in 
constrained household environments while remaining limited by tight coupling to specific robot platforms, single-modality input, lack of 
high-level planning, and weak handling of complex language logic.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 机器人大模型深度报告", "url": 
"https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", "published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id":
"20260702152206957300_65e4d14a", "type": "Claim", "text": "Hierarchical control architectures that combine large language models for 
high-level planning with reinforcement learning for low-level action generation (e.g., two-layer Hi-Core designs) are recognized in recent 
materials as an important route for embodied intelligence, particularly for long-horizon, multi-step tasks.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], "citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855785973_336d63ca", "title": 
"大模型赋能的具身智能：自主决策和具身学习技术的全面最新综述-人工智能技术与咨询", "url": "https://www.longtengyatai.com/info/284", 
"source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-10-31T14:57:20"}]}, {"id": "20260702152207019875_58edd8db", "type": "Claim", "text":
   1.5   "Current end-to-end VLA-based embodied systems have not yet achieved a fully robust perception–decision–execution closed loop in 
real-world environments, showing limited generalization across embodiments, low success rates (often only 20–40%) on long-horizon household 
tasks, and practical difficulties in coordinating slow high-level planning (around 1–10 Hz) with much faster low-level body control (≥100 
Hz).", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": 
