"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152207298358_afe36cc1", "type": "Claim", "text": "Market-oriented categorizations of embodied intelligence and humanoid robot teams 
typically distinguish three dominant technical lineages: (1) traditional hardware and motion-control–centric teams, (2) computer vision and 
autonomous driving–centric teams, and (3) large-model and reinforcement-learning–centric teams, with each lineage showing characteristic 
strengths and weaknesses across software, hardware, and commercialization capabilities.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], 
"citations": [5], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152427551438_6958bde6", "type": "Claim", "text": "From 1950–2000, 2000–2020, and since 2020, the development of embodied intelligence
is periodized respectively into a philosophy/concept phase, a technology accumulation phase, and a large‑model‑driven application expansion 
phase, with the post‑2020 era considered a new global inflection point.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 机器人大模型深度报告", "url": 
"https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", "published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id":
"20260702152427621617_1cb1fca9", "type": "Claim", "text": "Recent surveys and reports between 2024 and 2025 treat large models (LLMs, VLMs, 
VLA models) as a core technology route for embodied intelligence systems, and this route has been systematically reviewed in the 2025 Acta 
Automatica Sinica survey \"Embodied intelligence systems based on large models\".", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", 
"20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}, {"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152427814655_4a420513", "type": "Claim", "text": "One mainstream technical evolution route for embodied intelligence is the fusion of
generative AI with robot learning, progressing from traditional model
   1.6  ‑based and learning‑based motion control toward a \"large model + robot\" paradigm where LLMs handle task understanding and code 
generation, VLMs handle environment semantics, and VLA models generate end‑to‑end action policies.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": 
