"20260702152428251348_7a52b57a", "type": "Claim", "text": "Current end-to-end VLA (vision-language-action) models are recognized as a 
promising route for embodied intelligence but, as of 2025, they generally fail to realize a robust closed loop of 
perception–decision–execution in real environments, showing limited generalization across embodiments, low success rates (often 20–40%) on 
long-horizon tasks, and difficulties in software–hardware co-design due to disparate time scales between high-level planning (about 1–10 Hz) 
and low-level body control (≥100 Hz).", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
