"20260702152428402553_b7c1cdf0", "type": "Claim", "text": "Data-centric scaling laws constitute a cross-cutting methodological route for 
embodied foundation models: experiments such as ManiBox suggest spatial generalization performance scales as a power law with the spatial 
volume, implying that achieving 38× spatial generalization requires roughly 38^0.35 times more data and that each 10× increase in data volume 
yields approximately proportional performance gains.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": 
