"published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": "20260702160341158438_5ff39807", "type": "Claim", "text": "A prominent 2025 survey titled ‘Embodied 
intelligence systems based on large models’ in Acta Automatica Sinica systematically reviews embodied intelligence architectures that leverage
large models, focusing on large language models, large vision models, and foundational models for robot control and interaction.", 
"source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], "citations": [5], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": "20260702160341600481_1144f95d", "type": "Claim", "text": "The same large‑model survey identifies key 
unresolved research issues in the ‘brain’ layer of general embodied intelligence systems as of 2025, including challenges in model data scale 
and quality, training methodologies, inherent language model limitations, and reasoning optimization.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], "citations": [5], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": "20260702160341753410_36f5eeee", "type": "Claim", "text": "The large‑model survey and related industry
analyses argue that commercialization of general embodied intelligence still faces critical algorithmic and data bottlenecks in closing the 
‘perception–planning–control–execution’ loop, with end‑to‑end vision‑language‑action (VLA) models currently limited in generalization, 
long‑horizon task success rates, and cross‑platform transferability.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", 
"20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}, {"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702160341851914_253aab92", "type": "Claim", "text": "A widely cited experimental system, Google Robotics’ RT‑1 introduced in 2022, 
exemplifies an end‑to‑end Transformer‑based control route for embodied intelligence, achieving around 700 distinct tasks in home kitchen 
environments with an average success rate near 97% over 3000+ real tests, while still being constrained by strong coupling to its platform, 
single‑modality inputs, lack of high‑level planning, and limited parsing of complex language logic.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 
机器人大模型深度报告", "url": "https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", 
"published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id": "20260702160341918786_b24c79fa", "type": "Claim", "text": "Industry reports identify a distinct 
embodied intelligence route centered on the fusion of generative AI and robot learning, evolving from traditional model‑based and 
learning‑based motion control toward ‘large model + robot’ architectures where large language models perform task understanding and automatic 
code generation, vision‑language models handle semantic scene understanding, and vision‑language‑action models generate end‑to‑end action 
policies.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}, 
{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702160342017495_e764c768", "type": "Claim", "text": "Experimental and survey evide
  1.13  nce on data scaling, including ManiBox, suggests that for certain spatial manipulation tasks the amount of embodied data required for 
spatial generalization grows as a power law with the spatial volume, and that increasing data by roughly one order of magnitude tends to yield
proportional performance gains, highlighting data scale and quality as core enablers of embodied foundation models.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 
具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": "http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": 
"report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": "20260702160342131017_eedf4ee2", "type": "Claim", "text": "Reports characterize multi‑timescale 
control as a technical requirement for embodied intelligence systems, where high‑level task planning and decision components typically operate
at around 1–10 Hz, while low‑level body control loops need to run at 100 Hz or higher, creating nontrivial software–hardware co‑design 
challenges for end‑to‑end VLA and large‑model controllers.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": 
[{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702160342237142_b1ea04b7", "type": "Claim", "text": "A reinforcement‑learning‑centric technical route exemplified by architectures such 
as Hi‑Core uses hierarchical control where a large language model defines high‑level strategies and reinforcement learning generates low‑level
actions, blending symbolic task reasoning with continuous control for embodied agents.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], 
"citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855785973_336d63ca", "title": 
"大模型赋能的具身智能：自主决策和具身学习技术的全面最新综述-人工智能技术与咨询", "url": "https://www.longtengyatai.com/info/284", 
"source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-10-31T14:57:20"}]}, {"id": "20260702160342300770_5ffeee25", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 2024 
‘Composite Polymorphic Robots’ white paper by the Chinese Association for Artificial Intelligence identifies composite polymorphic robots, 
which integrate multiple forms or configurations, as an important technical path for embodied intelligence, arguing that their design concepts
and implementations are a necessary trend and market‑driven choice that help advance embodied intelligence capabilities.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], "citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855785973_336d63ca", "title": 
"大模型赋能的具身智能：自主决策和具身学习技术的全面最新综述-人工智能技术与咨询", "url": "https://www.longtengyatai.com/info/284", 
"source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-10-31T14:57:20"}]}, {"id": "20260702160342367836_f68a7466", "type": "Claim", "text": "Industry 
commentary and major corporate strategies (e.g., NVIDIA, Tesla, OpenAI) frame embodied intelligence—especially general humanoid robots—as the 
‘next frontier’ of AI, anticipating a potential ‘ChatGPT moment’ for humanoid robots and driving concentrated global investment and project 
prioritization in embodied AI.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], "citations": [6, 8], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
