"行业报告认为，具身智能的发展历程可被划分为1950–2000年的哲学与概念提出期、2000–2020年的技术积累期以及自2020年以来由大模型驱动的应用拓展期，这
一“以大模型驱动应用拓展”为特征的阶段也塑造了当前以端到端控制、大模型+机器人融合等具身智能技术路线的集中涌现。", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 
机器人大模型深度报告", "url": "https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", 
"published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id": "20260702151938981535_91ca056d", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"截至2025年初，通用具身智能的商业化技术路线在落地过程中普遍面临感知、规划、控制、执行闭环算法和高质量具身数据匮乏等关键挑战，这对端到端VLA、大
模型+机器人融合以及层级LLM+RL等路线的商业部署形成共性技术约束。", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", 
"20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}, {"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152206467988_44877720", "type": "Claim", "text": "From 2020 onward, the development of embodied intelligence is characterized by a 
new application expansion phase driven by large AI models, following earlier phases of philosophical/conceptual discussion (1950–2000) and 
technical accumulation (2000–2020).", "source_ids": ["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 机器人大模型深度报告", "url": 
"https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", "published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id":
"20260702152206532460_3e9ed5df", "type": "Claim", "text": "Recent surveys on large-model-based embodied intelligence systems treat the 
LLM/VLM-centric stack as a core technical route and explicitly use keywords such as large language model, large visual model, foundation 
model, embodied intelligence, and robot to structure the taxonomy.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", 
"20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}, {"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152206683708_34f6b5d3", "type": "Claim", "text": "The large‑model survey in Acta Automatica Sinica (2025, 51(1):1–19, 
doi:10.16383/j.aas.c240542) introduces a simplified technical stack for general embodied intelligence robots comprising ‘brain’, ‘cerebellum’,
and ‘body’, where the body technology is relatively mature but becomes significantly more complex and costly when high‑degree‑of‑freedom 
elements such as dexterous hands are added, placing greater demands on high‑speed communication and computation.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], "citations": [5], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": "20260702152206745904_0cd0af28", "type": "Claim", "text": "Another white paper identifies composite 
multi-mode robots as a distinct technical route within embodied intelligence, arguing that multi-form-factor design and implementation are 
both a natural direction of robotics technology and a market-driven choice, and that such composite robots are actively promoting embodied 
intelligence.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], "citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855785973_336d63ca", 
"t
   1.9  itle": "大模型赋能的具身智能：自主决策和具身学习技术的全面最新综述-人工智能技术与咨询", "url": 
"https://www.longtengyatai.com/info/284", "source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-10-31T14:57:20"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152206817777_f56df601", "type": "Claim", "text": "The technical evolution route of embodied intelligence described in a 2024–2025 
industry report starts from traditional model-based and learning-based motion control and transitions to a ‘large model + robot’ paradigm, in 
which large language models handle task understanding and automatic code generation, vision–language models handle semantic environment 
understanding, and vision–language–action models generate end-to-end action policies.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], 
"citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152206889056_adb64068", "type": "Claim", "text": "End-to-end transformer-based vision–language–action control models such as Google 
Robotics’ RT-1 constitute a major technical route for embodied intelligence, achieving high success rates and semantic generalization in 
constrained household environments while remaining limited by tight coupling to specific robot platforms, single-modality input, lack of 
high-level planning, and weak handling of complex language logic.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 机器人大模型深度报告", "url": 
"https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", "published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id":
"20260702152206957300_65e4d14a", "type": "Claim", "text": "Hierarchical control architectures that combine large language models for 
high-level planning with reinforcement learning for low-level action generation (e.g., two-layer Hi-Core designs) are recognized in recent 
materials as an important route for embodied intelligence, particularly for long-horizon, multi-step tasks.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], "citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855785973_336d63ca", "title": 
"大模型赋能的具身智能：自主决策和具身学习技术的全面最新综述-人工智能技术与咨询", "url": "https://www.longtengyatai.com/info/284", 
"source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-10-31T14:57:20"}]}, {"id": "20260702152207019875_58edd8db", "type": "Claim", "text": "Current 
end-to-end VLA-based embodied systems have not yet achieved a fully robust perception–decision–execution closed loop in real-world 
environments, showing limited generalization across embodiments, low success rates (often only 20–40%) on long-horizon household tasks, and 
practical difficulties in coordinating slow high-level planning (around 1–10 Hz) with much faster low-level body control (≥100 Hz).", 
"source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 
具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": "http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": 
"report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": "20260702152207114798_3745c70c", "type": "Claim", "text": "High-quality, ultra-large-scale embodied 
datasets are identified as a foundational enabler for embodied foundation models, with cited ManiBox-style research indicating a power-law 
relationship between spatial generalization volume and required data, such that achieving 38× spatial generalization demands roughly 38^0.35× 
more data, and each tenfold increase in data can yield roughly proportional performance gains under the studied settings.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 
具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": "http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": 
"report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": "20260702152207206666_aa7d7528", "type": "Claim", "text": "Industry analyses of general embodied 
intelligence emphasize that closing the full ‘perception–planning–control–execution’ loop and obtaining sufficient high-quality closed-loop 
data remain central technical bottlenecks for commercialization as of early 2025.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", 
"20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}, {"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152207298358_afe36cc1", "type": "Claim", "text": "Market-oriented categorizations of e
  1.10  mbodied intelligence and humanoid robot teams typically distinguish three dominant technical lineages: (1) traditional hardware and 
motion-control–centric teams, (2) computer vision and autonomous driving–centric teams, and (3) large-model and reinforcement-learning–centric
teams, with each lineage showing characteristic strengths and weaknesses across software, hardware, and commercialization capabilities.", 
"source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], "citations": [5], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": 
"基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": "https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", 
"published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": "20260702152427551438_6958bde6", "type": "Claim", "text": "From 1950–2000, 2000–2020, and since 2020, 
the development of embodied intelligence is periodized respectively into a philosophy/concept phase, a technology accumulation phase, and a 
large‑model‑driven application expansion phase, with the post‑2020 era considered a new global inflection point.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 
机器人大模型深度报告", "url": "https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", 
"published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id": "20260702152427621617_1cb1fca9", "type": "Claim", "text": "Recent surveys and reports between 2024 and
2025 treat large models (LLMs, VLMs, VLA models) as a core technology route for embodied intelligence systems, and this route has been 
systematically reviewed in the 2025 Acta Automatica Sinica survey \"Embodied intelligence systems based on large models\".", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}, 
{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152427814655_4a420513", "type": "Claim", "text": "One mainstream technical evolution route for embodied intelligence is the fusion of
generative AI with robot learning, progressing from traditional model‑based and learning‑based motion control toward a \"large model + robot\"
paradigm where LLMs handle task understanding and code generation, VLMs handle environment semantics, and VLA models generate end‑to‑end 
action policies.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": 
[{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}, 
{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152427930779_3e1748c7", "type": "Claim", "text": "Technical analyses of general embodied intelligence robots commonly decompose the 
system stack into \"brain–cerebellum–body\", where the body (mechanical and actuators) is relatively mature but becomes significantly more 
complex and costly when high‑DOF components such as dexterous hands are introduced, while the \"brain\" (large-model-based cognition and 
decision) remains largely at laboratory R&D stage with open issues in data, training methods, inherent language‑model limitations and 
reasoning optimization.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], "citations": [5], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152428025495_63c8cedd", "type": "Claim", "text": "Industry reports classify embodied-intelligence and humanoid-robot startup teams 
into three main technical‑gene routes: (1) traditional hardware and motion-control background, (2) computer-vision and autonomous-driving 
background, and (3) large-model and reinforcement-learning background, with each route exhibiting different strengths and weaknesses across 
software, hardware, and commercialization capabilities.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], "citations": [5], "sources": 
[{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152428115562_d3e8a03f", "type": "Claim", "text
  1.11  ": "End-to-end transformer-based control models such as Google Robotics RT‑1 represent a distinct embodied-intelligence route where a 
single model maps multimodal observations directly to actions; RT‑1 has demonstrated high success rates (around 97% over 3000 real tests on 
over 700 kitchen tasks) and strong semantic generalization in constrained household settings, but remains limited by platform coupling, 
single-modality inputs, lack of high-level planning, and insufficient handling of complex language logic.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 
机器人大模型深度报告", "url": "https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", 
"published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id": "20260702152428183867_3c1899a5", "type": "Claim", "text": "A hierarchical 
large-model-plus-reinforcement-learning route for embodied control is exemplified by Hi-Core style architectures, in which a large language 
model plans high-level strategies while a reinforcement-learning module generates low-level actions, forming a two-layer control hierarchy.", 
"source_ids": ["20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], "citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855785973_336d63ca", "title": 
"大模型赋能的具身智能：自主决策和具身学习技术的全面最新综述-人工智能技术与咨询", "url": "https://www.longtengyatai.com/info/284", 
"source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-10-31T14:57:20"}]}, {"id": "20260702152428251348_7a52b57a", "type": "Claim", "text": "Current 
end-to-end VLA (vision-language-action) models are recognized as a promising route for embodied intelligence but, as of 2025, they generally 
fail to realize a robust closed loop of perception–decision–execution in real environments, showing limited generalization across embodiments,
low success rates (often 20–40%) on long-horizon tasks, and difficulties in software–hardware co-design due to disparate time scales between 
high-level planning (about 1–10 Hz) and low-level body control (≥100 Hz).", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6],
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
