"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", "source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152820000645_4d4d85f9", "type": "Claim", "text": "A surveyed large‑model‑centric route to embodied intelligence treats the system as 
a hierarchy of \"brain–cerebellum–body\", where the body hardware is relatively mature but adding dexterous high‑degree‑of‑freedom components 
increases communication and compute demands and shifts key constraints toward cost.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855672073_474a9cc4"], 
"citations": [5], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855672073_474a9cc4", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702152820067332_852ceb6d", "type": "Claim", "text": "A major embodied intelligence route between 2022–2025 is end‑to‑end 
Transformer‑based control, exemplified by Google Robotics' RT‑1 model, which learns a direct mapping from multimodal inputs to actions and can
perform hundreds of household tasks with high success rates under constrained platforms and scenes.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 
