{"id": "20260702152207019875_58edd8db", "type": "Claim", "text": "Current end-to-end VLA-based embodied systems have not yet achieved a fully 
robust perception–decision–execution closed loop in real-world environments, showing limited generalization across embodiments, low success 
rates (often only 20–40%) on long-horizon household tasks, and practical difficulties in coordinating slow high-level planning (around 1–10 
Hz) with much faster low-level body control (≥100 Hz).", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6], "sources": 
[{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
