module generates low-level actions, forming a two-layer control hierarchy.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855785973_336d63ca"], "citations": 
[8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855785973_336d63ca", "title": 
"大模型赋能的具身智能：自主决策和具身学习技术的全面最新综述-人工智能技术与咨询", "url": "https://www.longtengyatai.com/info/284", 
"source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-10-31T14:57:20"}]}, {"id": "20260702152428251348_7a52b57a", "type": "Claim", "text": "Current 
end-to-end VLA (vision-language-action) models are recognized as a promising route for embodied intelligence but, as of 2025, they generally 
fail to realize a robust closed loop of perception–decision–execution in real environments, showing limited generalization across embodiments,
low success rates (often 20–40%) on long-horizon tasks, and difficulties in software–hardware co-design due to disparate time scales between 
high-level planning (about 1–10 Hz) and low-level body control (≥100 Hz).", "source_ids": ["20260702151855707416_0f6d4507"], "citations": [6],
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855707416_0f6d4507", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
