"20260702172831614366_c002e3b9", "type": "Claim", "text": "The RT-1 model released by Google Robotics in 2022 is an end-to-end 
Transformer-based robot control 
  1.11  model trained on approximately 130,000 teleoperation trajectories covering over 700 tasks in household kitchen scenarios, achieving 
around 97% average success in more than 3,000 real-world tests, while remaining limited by platform coupling, single modality, lack of 
high-level planning, and weak handling of complex language logic.", "source_ids": ["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 机器人大模型深度报告", "url": 
"https://pdf.dfcfw.com/pdf/H3_AP202508091724252221_1.pdf?1754816055000.pdf=", "source_type": "report", "published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id":
"20260702172831678023_9dc85688", "type": "Claim", "text": "Google’s SayCan framework, proposed in 2022, combines a language model with a 
feasibility model for robotic task planning in a two-stage architecture that achieved about 81% planning success and 60% execution success 
over 101 tasks in a real-world kitchen, but faces deployment limitations because its language and feasibility components are trained 
separately, require new annotation per environment, and lack autonomous re-planning for task sequences.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 
