"published_at": "2025-08-09"}]}, {"id": "20260702172831773744_e5c9743e", "type": "Claim", "text": "Google’s RT-2 model implements an 
end-to-end vision-language-action (VLA) architecture by discretizing continuous robot joint motions into 256 buckets per degree of freedom and
encoding them as rare textual tokens inserted into a PaLM-E-based vision-language model, which improves action generalization but yields 
action outputs at only about 1–5 Hz, insufficient for many complex real-world control scenarios.", "source_ids": 
["20260702151855743850_af5e94da"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702151855743850_af5e94da", "title": "[PDF] 
